# SendGrid `/api/sendgrid` block list

Before `sgMail.send`, the route must check `blocked-emails.json` via `extractEmail(from)` / `blockedEmails.has(...)`.

- Keep the list in `app/api/sendgrid/blocked-emails.json` (imported into `route.js`).
- Keep silent `200` on block (no SendGrid call).
- Keep `extractEmail` so `Name <email@x.com>` still matches.
- Forward remains: to `info@tu.biz`, from `edgar@teams.tu.biz`, replyTo = submitter.
- This does **not** block normal email to team mailboxes — only POSTs to this API.
